  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA, pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% acc, while config_010 (image, resnet50, singleprofile) achieves only 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. The key uncertainty is whether multiprofile aggregation (averaging multiple cell profiles per sample) can improve upon the singleprofile baseline. This experiment (config_002: RNA, pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) is the minimal extension of our best result, isolating the single→multi profile change while keeping the encoder fixed. It tests a fundamental architectural dimension that gates all downstream multimodal experiments (which require an aggregation strategy). Using avgpool first is the more robust, lower-variance choice compared to transformer aggregation, giving a clean baseline before exploring more complex aggregators. Under a tight budget, this single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about whether the multiprofile design axis is worth pursuing, directly informing whether to invest remaining experiments in multiprofile+fusion variants or to focus on encoder improvements."
